From: liuqin integration <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: quiet duplicate handover IRQ

The firmware can leave the handover interrupt asserted after the first
handover. The handler already ignores subsequent interrupts; reporting that
expected condition at error level floods the boot journal without indicating a
remoteproc failure.

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,6 +165,6 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		dev_dbg(q6v5->dev, "duplicate handover signal\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
